WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-How are you?

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.536 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am well, I am well.
I am well.

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.774
-Very happy that you found time
in what I assume

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
is an incredibly busy schedule
to be here with us.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.079
-I'm glad to be with you.
-It's a question I'm gonna

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.948 line:92%
try to ask everyone who is here,

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is trying to do
what you're doing.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of Senators
are running for president,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of your colleagues,
where you still work.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to go
to work with them.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Is it awkward...

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
...when you see each other?

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.830
-You know, no, it's actually --
I mean, so far so good.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-I think that all of us have

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.101 line:92%
a lot of respect for each other,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
and many of us
have worked together,

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.939
certainly since I've been there
the last two years.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:42.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, so far so good.
-All right.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.877 line:92%
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope it doesn't
end in fisticuffs.

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:49.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-You were a district attorney,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.052
both in San Francisco
and for the State of California,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.254
so you have a prosecutorial
background which, I think,

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of people have noticed
in committee hearings.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are very good
at asking questions.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Do you feel like

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.329
these questions, at this point,
and the kind of questions

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Trump administration
is being asked now

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
are making
the President nervous?

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or is this just how he is?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.640 line:92%
-I mean, here's the thing, Seth.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I'm there
asking those questions,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:19.512
it is because I believe the
American people want the truth.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:24.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sometimes you have to
extract the truth from people.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:28.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, you know, but we gotta
go where we have to go

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get at what's going on,
what has happened.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:34.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's how I think
of my role in those hearings.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you have to walk
sort of a sensitive line here,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you're on the
Senate Intelligence Committee,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you've seen things
that maybe aren't public.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:46.206
And we're in a situation now
where we have a Mueller report

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's out but not public.
-Right.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have a letter
from Attorney General Barr.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:54.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does it square,
what the four-page letter

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:57.217 line:92%
Barr put out with what you know?

00:01:57.217 --> 00:02:00.186 line:92%
-Well, put aside what I know.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think what
the American public knows

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:06.192
is that Bob Mueller was engaged
with an incredible team

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
for two years
in an investigation.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.165 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And the Attorney General

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
produced a four-page document
in two days.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.537 size:88% position:44%
And so, I think everyone
is smart enough to know

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.773
how could he possibly have
summarized two years worth

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
of around-the-clock
investigations

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
in two days
into just four pages?

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.813 size:75% position:38%
And for that reason,
I think we all know

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
we need to have
full transparency.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
The American public
deserves to see and know

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
what that investigation
involves.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:33.920 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.560
-I will say -- and this is a --
this is nonpartisan observation.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.195 line:92%
Nothing happens quickly in D.C.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:44.864
The fact that it was two days
later, he's like, "Good news.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got your answer.
It's nothing,"

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:47.901 line:92%
was very surprising to me.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:51.971
But I also want to ask,
are you surprised, disappointed,

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:55.408
that Mueller did have these two
years and it seems as though,

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:58.378
you know, some people have used
the expression that he punted

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:00.880 line:92%
on the decision whether or not

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was enough evidence
for obstruction.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel as though
an investigator

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.053 size:81% position:41%
who had that much time
and that much freedom

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
should have come
to a more concrete answer

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.256 align:start size:94% position:6%
on that question?
-Well, but we don't know

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.959
what Mueller said because
we've not seen the report,

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.227 line:92%
and that's part of the issue.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
The American public
and certainly

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
the United States Congress
should have the ability

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:21.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
to judge for itself
what the evidence was,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:24.804
what was the underlying evidence
that supported the report,

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:28.942
and there should be no hesitancy
by this administration,

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:31.377
certainly this Attorney General,
in giving it to us.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is a matter
of serious concern.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
And then we'll see.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:39.752
You know, I think that
there's every reason to believe,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on his entire career,
that Bob Mueller was thorough,

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he went
where the evidence took him.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.859 size:84% position:42%
But we need to see it,
because the other thing

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:50.263
I know as a prosecutor is that
there is a difference between

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:53.900
knowing what happened and being
able to prove what happened.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't mean
there's no evidence,

00:03:56.369 --> 00:04:00.006
but it probably means that there
was not sufficient evidence

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
to maybe
bring certain charges.

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:05.878
But let's not also forget,
there have been 33 indictments.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Let's not forget

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.249 line:92%
that there is a whole lot

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.717 size:78% position:39%
of evidence of crimes
that have happened,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people are taking
a toothbrush

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the courtroom these days
because of it.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:18.658
-Are you shocked as a prosecutor
how quickly it does seem like

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to remind people
how many people

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
who were close to
or worked explicitly

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.265 line:92%
for the Trump administration

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:29.535 size:81% position:41%
are either in prison
or have been arrested?

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.104 line:92%
-I mean, I think that it is --

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If I had asked you
this question four years ago

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said, "There will be
somebody in office and they'll

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.610
have this many people connected
to them in jail..."

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is quite unbelievable.
-Yeah. Right?

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, good.
-You're right.

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:43.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, good.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I thought I was crazy.
-No, no.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.388
And, actually, that's the thing
is that we all have to remember

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we are not crazy.
-Yeah.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:54.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that these are serious,
serious matters.

